# Docs & site sync on commit

Whenever you **create a git commit** (or the user asks to commit), treat documentation as part of the same change — do not leave public copy stale.

## Before finishing the commit

1. **Diff the change set** (`git diff` / staged files) and ask: does this alter user-facing behavior, setup, branding, env vars, Railway/deploy steps, dashboard features, strategy knobs, or public URLs?
2. If **yes**, update the matching surfaces in the **same commit** (or a follow-up commit in the same turn before you declare done). If **no**, note that briefly and skip.
3. Prefer **surgical edits** — only the sections that drifted. Do not rewrite unrelated docs.

## Surfaces to check (in order)

| Surface | Path | Update when… |
|---------|------|----------------|
| Marketing site | `docs/index.html`, `docs/assets/*` | Positioning, features, CTAs, branding, pricing/setup claims |
| Setup docs | `docs/setup/**` (`index`, `easy`, `advanced`) | Deploy/Railway/PM2/env/wizard/wallet steps change |
| LLM indexes | `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt` (repo root; create if missing) | Public product facts, URLs, setup summary, or feature list change |
| README | `README.md` | Install, quickstart, links, or project description change |
| Strategy / deploy notes | `STRATEGY.md`, `DEPLOY.md` | Only if the commit actually changes those workflows |

`llms.txt` = short machine-readable map (links + 1-line descriptions).  
`llms-full.txt` = fuller plain-text summary for crawlers/agents. Keep both factual and current with **DLMM Bot** / `dlmmbot.com` branding.

## Triggers that almost always need a docs pass

- New/changed setup wizard, wallet encryption, Settings, or Railway start behavior
- Renames/branding (product name, domain, repo URL)
- New env vars or required config keys users must set
- New dashboard capabilities called out on the marketing site
- Changes to easy vs advanced install paths

## Do not

- Skip docs because “we can update later” unless the user explicitly says so
- Paste secrets, private keys, or live `DASH_TOKEN` values into docs/llms files
- Expand scope into unrelated README/STRATEGY rewrites

## Done means

Commit includes code **and** any required doc/site/llms updates (or an explicit “no doc impact” judgment for that diff).
